I have gathered everything needed. Here is the complete map of the owner-creation pipeline.

## 1. The POST /owners YAML

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`**
```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

validate:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.ValidateOwnerFields
  next: build

build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save

save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond

respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerCreated
  govern: [ transaction ]
```
The pipeline is: **ValidateOwnerFields → BuildOwner → SaveOwner → RespondWithOwnerCreated**. (Companion list endpoint `owners.GET.yml` uses `ListOwners` with `readonly-transaction`.)

## 2. Java function classes referenced by the YAML

All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`

**`ValidateOwnerFields.java`** — this is where telephone normalization lives:
```java
public void service(@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated)
        throws MissingOwnerFieldsException, InvalidTelephoneException {
    List<String> missing = new ArrayList<>();
    require("firstName", request.getFirstName(), missing);
    require("lastName", request.getLastName(), missing);
    require("address", request.getAddress(), missing);
    require("city", request.getCity(), missing);
    require("telephone", request.getTelephone(), missing);
    if (!missing.isEmpty()) {
        throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing);
    }
    String telephone = request.getTelephone().replaceAll("\\D", "");
    if (telephone.length() != 10) {
        throw new InvalidTelephoneException(request.getTelephone());
    }
    request.setTelephone(telephone);
    validated.set(request);
}
private static void require(String field, String value, List<String> missing) {
    if (value == null || value.isBlank()) { missing.add(field); }
}
```
Note the officefloor pattern: the body is bound once with `@RequestBody`, then republished via `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>` and consumed downstream with `@Val` (a second `@RequestBody` binding would fail at runtime — see AGENTS.md).

**`BuildOwner.java`**
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
    built.set(ownerMapper.toOwner(request));
}
```

**`SaveOwner.java`**
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```

**`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`**
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper,
        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>> response) {
    OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
}
```

## 3. Owner entity and OwnerRepository

**Entity: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`** — extends `Person` (which holds firstName/lastName). Fields: `address` (`@NotEmpty`), `city` (`@NotEmpty`), `telephone`, and a `Set<Pet> pets`. Telephone bean-validation constraints:
```java
@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)
@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")
private String telephone;
```
Getters/setters: `getTelephone()/setTelephone()`, `getAddress()/setAddress()`, `getCity()/setCity()`, plus pets helpers `getPet(...)`, `addPet(...)`.

**Repository interface: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`**. Available methods (no telephone-specific query exists — only lastName lookups):
```java
Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName) throws DataAccessException;
Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable pageable) throws DataAccessException;
Owner findById(int id) throws DataAccessException;
void save(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException;
Collection<Owner> findAll() throws DataAccessException;
Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable pageable) throws DataAccessException;
void delete(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException;
```
There is **no** `findByTelephone` — if you need duplicate-telephone detection you would add a method here (and to the three impls) or filter `findAll()`. Implementations exist for JDBC/JPA/SpringData:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java`

## 4. Owner DTOs (the "Request/Response" equivalents)

There is **no** `OwnerRequest`/`OwnerResponse`. The DTOs are named **`OwnerFieldsDto`** (input) and **`OwnerDto`** (output), plus `OwnerPageDto`. They are **generated at build time** by the openapi-generator-maven-plugin from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java`, package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto` (configured at pom.xml lines 369-424). They do not exist as source files — to change DTO fields you edit `openapi.yml`.

Relevant schema in **`openapi.yml`** (lines 1991-2063):
- `OwnerFields` (→ `OwnerFieldsDto`): `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` — all required. `telephone` is `type: string`, `minLength: 1`, `maxLength: 20`, `pattern: '^[0-9]*$'`, example `'6085551023'`.
- `Owner` (→ `OwnerDto`): `allOf` OwnerFields plus read-only `id` (int32) and `pets` (array, required).

**Mapper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** (MapStruct, `componentModel=spring`):
```java
OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);
Owner toOwner(OwnerDto ownerDto);
@Mapping(target = "id", ignore = true) @Mapping(target = "pets", ignore = true)
Owner toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerDto);
List<OwnerDto> toOwnerDtoCollection(Collection<Owner> ownerCollection);
Collection<Owner> toOwners(Collection<OwnerDto> ownerDtos);
default OwnerPageDto toOwnerPageDto(Page<Owner> ownerPage) { ... }
```

## 5. Escalation handlers under officefloor/escalation/

YAMLs in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/` map an exception FQN (the filename) to a handler `class`:

| YAML (exception) | Handler class |
|---|---|
| `...escalation.NotFoundException.yml` | `NotFoundExceptionHandler` → 404 empty |
| `...escalation.InvalidTelephoneException.yml` | `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler` → 400 `{"errors":["telephone"]}` |
| `...escalation.MissingOwnerFieldsException.yml` | `MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler` → 400 `{"errors":[<fields>]}` |
| `org.springframework.dao.DataIntegrityViolationException.yml` | `DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler` → 404 ProblemDetail |
| `org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml` | `ValidationExceptionHandler` → 400 ProblemDetail w/ schemaValidationErrors |
| `org.springframework.security.authorization.AuthorizationDeniedException.yml` | `ForbiddenExceptionHandler` → 403 ProblemDetail |
| `java.lang.Exception.yml` | `GeneralExceptionHandler` → 500 ProblemDetail |

